  "kind": "new finite construction",
  "attribution_note": "Classical rectangular cells, cubical symmetry and guillotine composition, with no finite published donor packing. PingYou Ltd supplies the explicit finite whole-owner assemblies and certificates.",
  "construction": {
   "name": "complete_row_and_layer_prism_return",
   "proof": "COMPLETE ROW-AND-LAYER RETURN\n\nContinue the mixed-axis layer construction by allowing a layer itself to\ncompose two kinds of complete rows. This changes the finite physical\nassembly; owner angles still belong to the six fixed axis permutations\nof the predeclared prism frame.\n\nIn a layer whose vertical cell dimension is c, let its two remaining\nintrinsic cell dimensions be a,b. A type-0 row is b high and has\nfloor(S/a) whole cells, while a type-1 row is a high and has floor(S/b)\nwhole cells. The row word (i,j) has actual height i*b+j*a, and is legal\nwhen that height<=the SAME side S used for the horizontal rows. Its\ncapacity is i*floor(S/a)+j*floor(S/b). Each row is centered horizontally;\nthe complete collection of rows is centered vertically in its layer.\n\nCompose layers of the three possible vertical dimensions exactly as in\nMIXED_LAYER_PROOF.txt. Each complete row cell, every row boundary, each\nlayer boundary, and the one common cube side is retained. Nonoverlap is\nby z between layers, y between rows in a layer, and x within each row.\nThe retained owner words give a complete inverse map from this integer\ncomposition to actual centers and one of six proper cube-symmetry frames.\n\nEvery metric event arises from an integer row height, a horizontal cell\nmultiple, or a layer-height sum. The finite probe uses the first two as\ntransverse events, computes the two-type row capacity for each possible\nlayer type, and then enumerates layer words. Its realized common side is\nmax(transverse_event,total_layer_height); no layer chooses another side.\n\nThe native construction recomputes rigorous complete-owner boxes for all\nsix exact numeric quaternions and chooses shared outward rational cell\nwidths. Thus the nominal equations are never used as a substitute for a\ncomplete physical packing. Cartesian rows, layers and cubical symmetry\noperations are classical; the new contribution is the finite assembly\nand its verified witness against the pinned current records.\n",
